<task id="139" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C4 grant model — Collaborate/Full Access POA shares carry ShareAccess so OOB sharing matches Grant Access; every grant capped at the grantor's own level; superseded "No re-share" docs/tests rewritten</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27 — owner decisions round 2, grant-model group)</phase>
    <gate>after-138 (shares GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs, the write-time policy check and the modal)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the rights every internal POA share carries and the level every grant endpoint writes. Authorization-path .cs, tags bff-api/auth/pcf; existing characterization tests that pin the superseded rule must be rewritten.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Two rights vocabularies meet here (Dataverse AccessMask bits vs Spaarke AccessRights flags; RecordShareLevels.cs:24-29, :100-116). A mis-paired bit silently grants Share or Delete. The narrowing path can also silently DOWNGRADE someone else's existing grant through the upsert.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs and AccessGrantModal.tsx after task 138; task 140 reuses the ceiling method this task adds. Also shares hot files with other pending tasks: ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs (133 C11 creator-share, 143, 144, 148, 149, 150), InternalShareEndpoints.cs (142, 143, 149), GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs (137, 142), AccessibleRecordSetService.cs (the deny entry point; 135, 136, 137, 141, 142, 143, 036), and AccessGrantModal.tsx (066/067 chain). Merge serially and run /conflict-check first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>138</deps>
