    <origin>Session 26 defect C4 (HIGH). Session 27 owner answers on C4 (round 1) and round 2 items 3 and Q1 ("cap every grant at the grantor's own level").</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Reconcile the grant model with the owner's 2026-09-30 rule, and stop capping grants on one route only. Rules:
- A systemuser with Write may share (Dataverse OOB) and may use Grant Access for users, contacts and organizations (B-14 is retained).
- View-only grantees cannot grant; Collaborate and Full Access grantees can.
- Every grant, on every route, is capped at the grantor's own level.

Make OOB sharing agree with Grant Access by giving the Collaborate and Full Access share levels the Share right. Apply the grantor-level cap to /grant and /invite-and-grant, including org-wide grants, and keep /share-user consistent. Rewrite every doc, comment and test that still states the superseded "No re-share at any level" rule.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: the external-access management group (DelegationRuleFilter, the grant core, the POA share seam), with Dataverse POA semantics.</role>

  <goal>After this task:
(1) The three POA levels are: View Only = Read; Collaborate = Read, Write, Append, AppendTo, Share; Full Access = Collaborate + Delete. No level carries Assign. The two rights vocabularies are paired right by right, including Share.
(2) Secure-provisioning colleagues receive exactly the creator's rights.
(3) /grant and /invite-and-grant cap the requested level at the caller's own level, computed from a fresh OBO probe by ONE method that task 140 reuses. They narrow and report, never silently lower an existing grant, and apply the same cap to org-wide grants.
(4) /share-user keeps its per-right intersection (stated decision: narrow) and never silently lowers an existing share.
(5) Contact and organization grantees on the record's No Access List are refused at write time with a message.
(6) DelegationRuleFilter and /can-manage-access still mean "Write on this record".
(7) Legacy shares written under the old masks keep their level on read, and an operator-run backfill upgrades them.
(8) Every artefact that states "No re-share" is rewritten.
(9) The behaviour is proven live at a manual gate.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>THE OWNER'S RULE (session 27, verbatim in substance; notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md:7, :19-21, :30):
- "If the user has write access, then they can share (OOB functionality) and grant access to users/contacts/organizations."
- "No re-share" and "grant what you hold" apply only to a principal holding View by virtue of a grant.
- Collaborate and Full Access carry grant-access ability.
- Q1: "cap every grant at the grantor's own level".
This SUPERSEDES the 2026-09-15 decision "No re-share at any level" (notes/task-063-internal-user-share-endpoints.md:94-105). B-14 (notes/design-register.md:84: you may grant if you hold Write) is RETAINED.

WHAT THE CODE SAYS TODAY (verified 2026-09-30):
- The delegation gate is Write only: `RequiredRight = AccessRights.Write` (Api/ExternalAccess/DelegationRuleFilter.cs:86; the only rights test is :170-179). That already matches the owner's rule for systemusers. It STAYS. DelegationRuleCharacterizationTests.cs:43-51 and :144-155 pin "Write delegates; Share does not substitute". Those pins remain TRUE and stay green.
- The POA levels carry no Share: ViewOnlyMask = Read, CollaborateMask = Read|Write|Append|AppendTo, FullAccessMask = +Delete (Services/Access/RecordShareLevels.cs:45-53). The remarks at :19-22 state "Share and Assign are at no level (owner, 'No re-share at any level')".
- The Dataverse bits are Read 1, Write 2, Append 4, AppendTo 16, Delete 65536, Share 262144 (:24-29).
- So a Collaborate sharee holds Write, and may grant through every Spaarke route. But they hold no ShareAccess, so they CANNOT use Dataverse's own Share in the MDA. The two surfaces disagree.
- The Intersect table (:109-116) has no Share row. Today Intersect DROPS any Share bit in a requested mask. Adding Share to a level without adding the row would silently strip it.
- Secure provisioning shares differently by principal:
  - the creator gets `CollaborateRights + ",ShareAccess"` (Api/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:169);
  - colleagues get `CollaborateRights` (:181);
  - the rationale comments at :158-181 ("re-sharing stays with the creator so the access list cannot widen through a chain nobody reviewed") state the opposite of the owner's rule.
  - The share calls are at :730 (creator) and :758 (colleagues).
- "Grant what you hold" exists ONLY on /share-user, as a per-right intersect-and-narrow (Api/ExternalAccess/InternalShareEndpoints.cs:261-311; the response carries `narrowed`). The remark at :50-51 says no level carries Share or Assign.
- /grant has no cap at all. AccessLevel is only Enum.IsDefined (GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:95-97), and org-wide grants are allowed (:84-87, :679-682). /invite-and-grant is the same (InviteAndGrantExternalUserEndpoint.cs:62-64, :114-128).
- 🔴 LATENT DOWNGRADE HAZARD, which the cap would make LIVE: CreateGrantAsync's match path updates the survivor's level IN PLACE to the requested level (GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:248-260). /share-user's write is ModifyAccess, which REPLACES rights (InternalShareEndpoints.cs:343-346). A naive cap would narrow "Full Access please" to Collaborate and then overwrite an existing Full Access grant somebody else made, lowering it while the caller asked for MORE.
- ExternalAccessLevels.ToDisplayLevel (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalCallerContext.cs:234-243) says "Display only. Never authorize on this", and its containment tests include Create. RetrievePrincipalAccess on a record is not guaranteed to report CreateAccess, so reusing it as a cap could under-state a Deep-role user as View Only. The ceiling needs its own named method over Read / Write / Delete only.
- Superseded artefacts that must be rewritten:
  - RecordShareLevels.cs:14-41 (remarks);
  - ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:158-181;
  - InternalShareEndpoints.cs:50-51;
  - tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/InternalUserShareTests.cs:258-271 ("No re-share" comment), :313-324 (Levels_NeverCarryShareOrAssign), :326-332 (CreatorMask outside the levels), :334-342 (creator vs colleague constants);
  - tests/integration/data-mutation/ExternalAccess/SecureProjectShareTests.cs:75-110 (colleagues WITHOUT ShareAccess);
  - notes/phase4-uat-acceptance.md:24 (U-3 "cannot re-share");
  - notes/design-register.md:84 (B-14 row; add the 2026-09-30 decision alongside it);
  - notes/task-063-internal-user-share-endpoints.md:94-105 (§4, "No re-share at any level") and tasks/063-internal-user-share-endpoints.poml:102 — add a SUPERSEDED banner pointing at the 2026-09-30 decision; keep the history text.
- 🟢 The pre-change CREATOR mask (Collaborate + Share = 262167, `InternalUserShareTests.cs:59`) is EXACTLY the new Collaborate mask. Existing secure-provisioning creator shares therefore read as Collaborate with no backfill; the backfill touches only colleague and "+ User" shares at the legacy 23 / 65559 masks.
- The Q5 "Assigned To" auto-grant function (task 142) writes through CreateGrantAsync with NO human grantor, which is why the ceiling lives in the /grant and /invite-and-grant HANDLERS (and task 140's contact route), not inside the core. Task 142 must still never lower an existing higher grant; cite this task's never-silently-lower rule to it.

LIVE FACTS (session 27):
- The Share privilege on project, matter and work assignment is held at Deep by "Spaarke Core User" and "Spaarke Office Add In User". So a Collaborate sharee with ShareAccess on the record can use MDA Share.
- Dataverse's native rule already stops an OOB sharer granting rights they do not hold.</background>
