  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 / B-14">Scope: DelegationRuleFilter and RecordAccessGateEndpoint.
- The delegation right stays Write, evaluated as the caller over OBO. Do not change DelegationRuleFilter.RequiredRight, its target resolution, or /can-manage-access semantics.
- DelegationRuleCharacterizationTests' existing Write pins and RecordAccessGateTests stay green with no assertion edits. Comment edits that cite the new decision are allowed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (C4)">Scope: RecordShareLevels.
- ViewOnlyMask = 1.
- CollaborateMask = 1|2|4|16|262144 = 262167.
- FullAccessMask = CollaborateMask|65536 = 327703.
- Assign (524288) is at no level.
- Share is added to the LevelRights pairing table as ("ShareAccess", 262144, AccessRights.Share), so Intersect carries it only when the caller holds AccessRights.Share.
- The levels still NEST (View ⊂ Collaborate ⊂ Full). The race-safety note at :35-40 depends on it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="data compatibility">Scope: RecordShareLevels.LevelForMask.
- The legacy masks written before this task MUST still read as their level: 23 → Collaborate and 65559 → Full Access. Otherwise /user-shares and the modal show "no level" for every existing share.
- Any other mask stays null.
- The legacy masks are upgraded by the backfill script, not rewritten on read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner Q1 — one ceiling">Scope: /grant, /invite-and-grant (this task) and task 140's contact route (reuse). The grantor's ceiling is ONE method on ExternalAccessLevels, over Spaarke AccessRights:
- Full Access iff Read + Write + Delete;
- Collaborate iff Read + Write;
- View Only iff Read;
- otherwise none.
Create, Append, AppendTo and Share are NOT consulted, because RetrievePrincipalAccess is not guaranteed to report CreateAccess for an existing record. Do not call ToDisplayLevel for this (its remark forbids authorizing on it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="stated decision: NARROW">Scope: all three routes. NARROW, do not refuse.
- A request above the caller's ceiling is written AT the ceiling.
- The response says so: additive DTO fields for the granted level and narrowed = true on /grant and /invite-and-grant; /share-user keeps its existing narrowed flag and per-right intersection, which is Dataverse's own sharing rule and never exceeds the grantor.
- A ceiling of none returns 403 with reasonCode `sdap.access.grant.caller_cannot_grant` on /grant and /invite-and-grant (/share-user keeps its existing `sdap.access.user_share.caller_cannot_grant`) and a readable detail. It IS reachable: the handler re-probes, and CallerRecordAccessProbe answers AccessRights.None — it does not throw — for every OBO, WhoAmI, transport and parse failure (CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:49-56, :450-487), so a transient failure on the second probe lands here. Nothing is written or onboarded.
- A probe that THROWS returns 500 ProblemDetails with a readable detail. Nothing is written and nothing is onboarded, mirroring InternalShareEndpoints.cs:280-288.
- The probe is re-run in the handler, not trusted from the filter, mirroring InternalShareEndpoints.cs:268-272.</constraint>
    <constraint source="data integrity: never silently lower">Scope: all three routes. When the cap narrowed the request (narrowed = true) AND the target already holds more than the narrowed result, refuse with 409 ProblemDetails and a readable detail ("they already have more access than you can grant"). Nothing is written.
- "Holds more" means: for a contact or org, an active grant row on the key whose level is higher; for a user, any right in the stored share mask that the narrowed mask lacks.
- An explicit request for a LOWER level (narrowed = false) is a deliberate downgrade by a Write-holder, allowed exactly as today.
- /invite-and-grant: the grantee Contact may not exist yet. BEFORE onboarding, resolve an EXISTING contact by the request email READ-ONLY (no create; the same match ProvisionAsync uses). If one exists, run the never-lower and deny-list checks against it; if none exists there is no existing row, and the deny-list check runs on the request's OrganizationId (the firm) only. Creating the contact first to obtain an id is forbidden: a refused request must leave no Contact and no CIAM account behind.
- This 409 carries the stable reasonCode `sdap.access.grant.would_lower_existing`. Task 140 reuses it verbatim.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner Q1 — org-wide">Scope: /grant org grants. The same ceiling applies to organization-wide grants. Task 138's policy check already refuses org grants on Secure, Limited and Restricted roots. This task does not duplicate that check; it runs after it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C4 fix direction / FR-23">Scope: /grant and /invite-and-grant. A grantee denied on this record by the No Access List is refused at write time with 422 ProblemDetails (reasonCode `sdap.access.grant.grantee_denied`, reused verbatim by task 140) and a readable detail. The grantee cases are: the contact itself; any of the contact's ACTIVE organizations; or, for an org grant, the organization.
- The check runs before any onboarding. Nothing is written or provisioned.
- The deny decision MUST come from the SAME code as the read-path deny veto (AccessibleRecordSetService.ResolveDenyVetoAsync, :596) through a narrow entry point. Do not re-implement the key shapes.
- A deny-list read fault is a refusal with a message (fail closed).
- Internal-user deny on /share-user is owner Q4 and belongs to task 143 (No Access List for internal users on secure records). Do not implement it here; name it in the notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (C4) — provisioning">Scope: ProvisionProjectEndpoint. Colleagues named at secure provisioning receive EXACTLY the creator's rights (the new Collaborate level, which now includes ShareAccess). Both constants derive from RecordShareLevels, and the tests assert them against the LITERAL CSV, per the existing discipline at InternalUserShareTests.cs:337-339.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests. Use the existing fixtures: DelegationRuleTestFixture's substituted probe, FakeRecordShareTable, ProvisionProjectTestFixture. Every new negative has a positive twin that differs only in the caller's rights, as the existing suite requires (DelegationRuleCharacterizationTests.cs:26-32).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner binding">Scope: live verification. A MANUAL gate on spaarkedev1 with existing non-admin test users in the correct BU. No relocation. No Dataverse credential in CI. The backfill script is run by the operator, dry-run first.
- The script authenticates with the operator's OWN identity (az / pac token, as scripts/Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1 does). It never uses or adds a client secret (ADR-028 A4).
- Its write scope is SYSTEMUSER principals at exactly 23 or 65559 on the three root tables. Team principals and any other mask are listed, never modified (escalation 3).
- Every ModifyAccess is read back, and the before/after counts are recorded.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 / ADR-028 A4">Scope: this task's PR.
- State placement (BFF; no new component beyond the named method, DTO fields and script).
- Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master worktree using the short-path, Compress-Archive, equal-file-count procedure. Ceiling 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.
- No new .WithClientSecret(...). GrantMembershipAsync stays at zero callers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner binding">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred. Discovered scope is added here.</constraint>
      <constraint source="main-session-review">WP-1 — the grantor ceiling, the never-lower rule and the deny/Restricted write-time refusals are enforced INSIDE the single grant-writing core (the method every grant writer calls to persist sprk_externalrecordaccess), as a REQUIRED ceiling parameter — never only in the /grant and /invite-and-grant handlers. No caller may persist a grant without passing a ceiling: 140 passes the contact grantor's effective level, 142's auto-grants pass an explicit documented Collaborate ceiling (owner Q5), and admin/system writers pass their own documented ceiling. An ArchTest or unit guard proves every call site supplies it (seed a call without it and watch the guard fail).</constraint>
</constraints>

  <adr-tensions>
    <tension adr="ADR-008 (resource authorization in endpoint filters)" path="C — comply (precedent)">
      <rule>Resource authorization is applied by endpoint filters at route registration.</rule>
      <conflict>The cap depends on the caller's rights on the record AND the requested level. It is a narrowing of the write, not an allow/deny decision. The allow/deny stays in DelegationRuleFilter.</conflict>
      <proposed>Keep the allow/deny in the filter and do the narrowing in the handler, exactly as task 063's /share-user does (InternalShareEndpoints.cs:261-311, already reviewed under ADR-008). No amendment is needed. Cite it in the PR.</proposed>
      <rejected>Moving the cap into DelegationRuleFilter: rejected, because the filter answers one question for every route on the group (including revoke, close-project and provision), and /can-manage-access reports its verdict verbatim. Level-awareness there would change the gate's meaning, which the owner told this task to keep as Write.</rejected>
    </tension>
    <tension adr="design decision 2026-09-15 'No re-share at any level' (not an ADR)" path="superseded by owner">
      <rule>notes/task-063-internal-user-share-endpoints.md:94-105.</rule>
      <proposed>Record the 2026-09-30 decision in notes/design-register.md next to B-14, with a "superseded" pointer from the task-063 note. Do not rewrite the task-063 history itself.</proposed>
    </tension>
  </adr-tensions>

  <justification>
    <existing>The ceiling: grep "ToDisplayLevel|GrantCeiling|Intersect\(" over src/server finds ExternalAccessLevels.ToDisplayLevel (ExternalCallerContext.cs:234, display-only) and RecordShareLevels.Intersect (RecordShareLevels.cs:132, POA masks only). There is no level ceiling over AccessRights. The DTO fields: GrantAccessResponse.cs:8 carries no level or narrowed flag. The backfill script: grep of scripts/ for "ModifyAccess" finds only Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1 (a schema script, no POA writes).</existing>
    <extension>The ceiling is a method ADDED to the existing ExternalAccessLevels class, not a new type. The response changes are additive fields on existing DTOs. The script is a new file, because no script enumerates principalobjectaccess rows. It follows Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1's shape (-DryRun default, idempotent, report-first).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the ceiling, a Collaborate sharee mints Full Access (including Delete they lack) or org-wide grants through /grant. Without the backfill, every colleague shared before this task keeps a mask without ShareAccess, so MDA Share stays unavailable to exactly the people the owner said may share. Without the DTO fields, a narrowed grant reports success at a level the caller did not get.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

