  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>1. Live verification shows RetrievePrincipalAccess (CallerRecordAccessProbe) does not report WriteAccess or DeleteAccess for a user whose role or share clearly grants them. The ceiling would then under-state real holders. STOP, record the live probe output, and escalate. Do not add Create/Append/Share to the ceiling test to compensate.</trigger>
    <trigger>2. Live verification shows a Collaborate sharee can use MDA Share to hand out a right they do not hold (for example Delete), contradicting Dataverse's documented behaviour. STOP. The owner's model assumes the platform caps OOB shares natively.</trigger>
    <trigger>3. The backfill dry-run finds shares whose mask is neither a current level nor a legacy level (for example a creator share that also carries Delete, or an Assign bit), or legacy-mask shares whose principal is a TEAM. Do not modify them. Report them per record and escalate for an owner decision. Recommendation: upgrade team shares at 23/65559 exactly like user shares (a team shared at Collaborate is the same owner-decided level), and leave every non-level mask untouched as a hand-made MDA share.</trigger>
    <trigger>4. Task 143 (owner Q4: the No Access List for internal users on secure records) has landed and expects /share-user to refuse denied systemusers. Coordinate through the main session rather than implementing a second deny check here.</trigger>
    <trigger>5. Task 133 (C11 creator lock-out) or task 144 (named secure owner team) has changed the provisioning share step in a way that conflicts with "creator rights = colleague rights = the Collaborate level". STOP and reconcile with that task's shipped code rather than overwriting it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

