  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. Level table.
- TryGetRights yields View Only ("ReadAccess", 1), Collaborate ("ReadAccess,WriteAccess,AppendAccess,AppendToAccess,ShareAccess", 262167) and Full Access (Collaborate CSV + ",DeleteAccess", 327703), asserted against LITERALS.
- No level's mask contains Assign (524288).
- LevelForMask maps 1, 262167, 327703, and the legacy 23 and 65559, to their levels. Every other mask maps to null.
- /share-user at Collaborate by a caller holding Read|Write|Append|AppendTo|Share, for a user whose stored mask is the legacy 23, writes ModifyAccess to 262167 and reports outcome "updated" (not "unchanged"); the same request by a caller WITHOUT Share writes nothing and reports "unchanged" (twin).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Pairing. Intersect(Full Access, callerRights) carries ShareAccess ONLY when callerRights contains AccessRights.Share. Every existing right-by-right pairing test still passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. Provisioning. The creator share and every colleague share carry the identical CSV (the new Collaborate literal, including ShareAccess). SecureProjectShareTests and InternalUserShareTests are rewritten to assert this. No test asserts "colleague without ShareAccess" any more.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. Ceiling method.
- Read+Write+Delete → Full Access; Read+Write → Collaborate; Read → View Only; None → null.
- The result does not change when Create, Append, AppendTo or Share are added or removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. /grant cap, contact.
- A caller probed at Read|Write (no Delete) requesting Full Access gets 200, a row written at Collaborate, and a response with granted level Collaborate and narrowed = true.
- The positive twin, a caller with Delete, gets Full Access with narrowed = false.
- /invite-and-grant behaves identically, with the ceiling computed before onboarding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. /grant cap, organization-wide. The same narrowing applies to an org grant on a Standard root.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. Never silently lower.
- On all three routes, when narrowing occurs and the target already holds a higher level or a wider mask, the result is 409 ProblemDetails (`sdap.access.grant.would_lower_existing`) with a readable detail and NO write (no UpdateAsync, no ModifyAccess).
- /invite-and-grant: the same 409 for an EXISTING contact (found by the read-only email match) is returned before onboarding; the onboarding seam is asserted not called and no contact is created.
- The positive twin, an explicit lower-level request with narrowed = false, still downgrades as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. Probe outcomes on /grant and /invite-and-grant:
- a probe that THROWS → 500 ProblemDetails with a readable detail;
- a probe that answers AccessRights.None on the handler's re-probe → 403 `sdap.access.grant.caller_cannot_grant` with a readable detail;
- in both cases no row is written and no contact or CIAM account is created (onboarding seam asserted not called).
- /share-user's existing behaviour is pinned alongside: a throwing probe → 500 `sdap.access.user_share.read_failed`, None → 403 `sdap.access.user_share.caller_cannot_grant`, no write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. Deny list at write time.
- A contact grantee on the record's No Access List, or whose active organization is on it, or an org grantee that is on it, gets 422 `sdap.access.grant.grantee_denied` with a readable detail and nothing written or onboarded.
- The positive twin, the same request for a non-denied grantee, succeeds.
- A deny-list read fault is a message-bearing refusal.
- The decision comes from the shared deny code path (asserted by using the real NoAccessListReader behind a substituted query, not a re-implementation).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Gate unchanged (negative/authorization).
- A Read-only caller on /grant, /invite-and-grant and /share-user still gets 403 delegation_write_required.
- EveryRightExceptWrite (including ShareAccess) still gets 403.
- RecordAccessGateTests pass with no assertion edits.
- DelegationRuleFilter.RequiredRight is still AccessRights.Write.
- Positive twin (new): a caller holding exactly the new Collaborate rights (Read, Write, Append, AppendTo, Share) passes the gate on /grant, /invite-and-grant, /share-user and /can-manage-access.
- /can-manage-access answers 200 for a Write-holder on a Restricted, a Limited and a Secure record alike (the flags govern grant TYPES at write time, task 138, not the gate), and 403 without Write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. Modal. jest asserts that a narrowed /grant or /invite-and-grant response renders the narrowed notice, and that a 409/422/403 ProblemDetails renders the server's detail text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. Superseded artefacts rewritten.
- RecordShareLevels remarks, ProvisionProjectEndpoint :158-181 and InternalShareEndpoints :50-51 state the 2026-09-30 rule.
- grep over src/ and tests/ (excluding generated bundle.js) for "No re-share", "re-sharing stays with the creator", "no level carries Share", "Share and Assign are at no level" and "WithoutShareAccess" returns 0 hits; the grep output is recorded in the notes.
- phase4-uat-acceptance.md U-3 reads: a colleague named at provisioning can read and edit, can share in MDA, and can use Manage Access, capped at their own level; a View Only sharee cannot.
- design-register.md keeps B-14 and records the 2026-09-30 decision. notes/task-063-internal-user-share-endpoints.md §4 and tasks/063 :102 carry a SUPERSEDED banner, with their history text kept.
- docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-ADMIN-SETUP.md carries a POA share-level table and describes the cap, narrowing and the never-lower 409. docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md states the same.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">13. MANUAL LIVE GATE on spaarkedev1, existing non-admin test users in the correct BU, results in notes:
(a) A colleague shared at Collaborate through "+ User" can open the project in MDA, use the MDA Share command on it (and the share it creates cannot include Delete), and open Manage Access (the gate returns 200).
(b) A colleague shared at View Only cannot open Manage Access (the gate returns 403) and has no MDA Share.
(c) A Collaborate colleague's /grant at Full Access writes Collaborate and the modal shows the narrowed notice.
(d) A newly provisioned secure project's colleague share mask equals the creator's (read from principalobjectaccess).
(e) The operator runs the backfill -DryRun and then for real. Counts are recorded, and a previously shared colleague can then use MDA Share.
(f) U-3 is run as rewritten.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">14. Build green. BFF unit + integration + NetArchTest green. jest green. PCF build:prod green. Publish-size delta reported per §10 (fresh master worktree, short path, equal file counts), ≤ 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">15. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above (level literals, legacy masks, Share pairing, ceiling table, narrow/no-narrow twins, never-lower twins, deny twins, probe fault, unchanged gate). Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

